Execute an arbitrary GraphQL query against a Shopify Admin API endpoint.

USAGE
  $ shopify store execute [-q <value>] [--query-file <value>] [-s <value>]
    [-v <value>] [--variable-file <value>] [--output-file <value>] [--version
    <value>] [--allow-mutations] [--json] [--no-color] [--verbose]

FLAGS
  -q, --query=<value>          The GraphQL query or mutation, as a string.
      --query-file=<value>     Path to a file containing the GraphQL query or
                               mutation. Can't be used with --query.
  -s, --store=<value>          The store to query (defaults to the active
                               store).
  -v, --variables=<value>      The values for any GraphQL variables in your
                               query or mutation, in JSON format.
      --variable-file=<value>  Path to a JSON file with variables (use for large
                               payloads).
      --output-file=<value>    The file name where results should be written,
                               instead of STDOUT.
      --version=<value>        The API version to use for the query or mutation.
                               Defaults to the latest stable version.
      --allow-mutations        Allow mutations to be executed (off by default
                               to prevent accidental writes to a live store).
      --json                   Compact JSON output.
      --no-color               Disable color output.
      --verbose                Increase the verbosity of the output.

EXAMPLES
  $ shopify store execute --query '{ shop { name } }'
  $ shopify store execute -q '{ shop { name } }' --output-file out.json
  $ shopify store execute --query-file query.graphql --variable-file vars.json --allow-mutations

DESCRIPTION
  Sends the query directly to /admin/api/<version>/graphql.json with the
  current store's bearer token. Use `shopify store auth` first to authenticate.

